  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Money Transit Map",
    "overview": "Finco's public landing page makes financial relationships feel navigable. Indigo destinations, quiet routing lines, and readable amounts turn an abstract financial picture into a route someone can inspect. The atmosphere is open, precise, and approachable: large Manrope statements sit beside a concrete illustration, while generous space keeps supporting explanations calm.\n\nThis system applies only to `/` and `src/components/landing/`. Its light palette is scoped by the landing stylesheet. The financial graph, dashboard, authentication screens, and shared application tokens keep their existing design; this document does not authorize changing them. The shared Finco mark is recolored locally on the landing page. Page sequence and campaign copy belong in `.impeccable/surfaces/landing.md`, rather than becoming rules for every future surface.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Light canvas with indigo actions and lilac illustration surfaces.",
      "One Manrope family, confident headlines, and legible financial amounts.",
      "Flat surfaces with crisp routes and restrained borders.",
      "Rounded action pills and distinct destination containers.",
      "Deliberate interaction with no autonomous landing motion."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Landing Boundary Rule",
        "body": "Apply these colors inside the landing surface only. Keep the node graph and shared application's existing tokens authoritative for their own screens.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Route Color Rule",
        "body": "Indigo identifies an action or a meaningful point in the financial route. Route strokes stay quieter than destinations and amounts.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Readable Destination Rule",
        "body": "Amounts lead within each destination, and the label explains the amount beside it. Preserve tabular numerals when values can change.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Map Rule",
        "body": "Use tonal surfaces and routing lines to establish hierarchy on this landing. A destination's color and content carry its importance.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Accounted Change Rule",
        "body": "When the savings control changes the example, savings and remaining money update together while monthly income and spending stay consistent. The annual difference must follow that same monthly change; visual feedback follows the calculation.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep the landing palette and component rules scoped to `/` and its landing components.",
      "**Do** pair financial route lines with readable destination labels and amounts.",
      "**Do** use tabular numerals for values that change in place.",
      "**Do** preserve visible keyboard focus and reduced-motion behavior.",
      "**Do** identify illustrative financial examples as demos.",
      "**Do** use flat tonal surfaces and open separators to keep explanations calm."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** replace shared dark application tokens or graph styling with this landing's light system.",
      "**Don't** animate the landing route continuously; interaction should follow a deliberate action.",
      "**Don't** turn every explanatory block into an enclosed card.",
      "**Don't** treat compact diagram annotations as the default size for reading text.",
      "**Don't** use color alone to explain a financial destination or changed amount."
